checks_run.procedure:
Extract the source rows straight from docs/source/playbook.md and compare them with the candidate's seeds and i18n:
- B0009 modes;
- B0018 roles;
- B0023 gates;
- B0035 charter fields;
- B0037 thesis;
- B0039-B0043 scope checks;
- B0029 workstreams;
- B0056 TOM dimensions;
- B0062 canvas.

D-073 from the domain angle, through the product's own routes:
- a normal upload with EN and AR file names;
- access reaching its effectiveTo while the body streams;
- an administrator revoking the assignment mid-stream through POST /role-assignments/{id}/revoke;
- the uploader signing out mid-stream;
- a later upload on the same items;
- localized refusal codes;
- dev sign-in for every seeded synthetic user.

In the browser, EN (LTR) and AR (RTL):
- (a) dev sign-in through the login form, sign-out, sign-in again;
- (b) upload a file through the Upload dialog, then download it through the page link.

Browser, EN and AR:
- the charter form-level JSON problem is shown once;
- Arabic charter text with RLM and emoji is created verbatim;
- an evidence upload through the dialog downloads unchanged.

Browser, EN and AR: the user-visible outcome when access is withdrawn and the upload is refused, and when a session ends while the app is open. Four probes:
- r13-ui (c) and r13-ui-withdrawn: an admin revokes before the upload is confirmed;
- r13-session-end-ui: sign-out elsewhere, then an in-app link, plus a reload control;
- the same with the product's default rate limits.

Check the D-073 change scope and the product invariants:
- product files changed since round 12;
- no i18n, migration, seed, catalogue, gate-rule or web change;
- no certification claim;
- gate codes;
- no float columns;
- the provisional brand token;
- DG0-DG7 mentions in product source.

